<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 68,782 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 68,782 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 68,782 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday, compared to 97,162 tonnes on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Thursday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			7,954	     16,747</p>
<p>    Import cargo			60,828	    80,415</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, three ships are expected to sail and six to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 9,300	 Vi Vi		     13/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		 4,000	 United Tina	     13/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		10,000	 Wawasan Courage	 due</p>
<p>Gas oil		 60,000	 Themera		   17/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
